# Multi-Sensor IoT Monitoring System

## Student Information

**Course:** Internet of Things (IoT) Lab

**Project:** Multi-Sensor IoT Monitoring System using ESP32

---

# Project Overview

This project implements a multi-sensor IoT monitoring system using an ESP32 programmed in MicroPython. The system collects data from multiple sensors, processes the data at the edge, and sends the processed information to Node-RED using HTTP.

Node-RED stores the data in InfluxDB, while Grafana displays the sensor readings through a real-time dashboard.

---

# Objectives

The objectives of this project are:

- Read multiple sensors using ESP32
- Apply moving average filtering to MQ-5 gas sensor readings
- Classify gas levels into SAFE, WARNING, and DANGER
- Detect fever using the MLX90614 infrared temperature sensor
- Read pressure and altitude from BMP280
- Obtain timestamps using the DS3231 RTC module
- Send processed data to Node-RED
- Store data in InfluxDB
- Visualize data using Grafana

